 "title": "Gene Expression and Chemical Analysis in Dendrobium officinale and Yeast Cells",
 "summary": "This cluster involves the analysis of gene expression in Dendrobium officinale and yeast cells. The DoMYB102 gene activates the expression of DoUGT71K2 in D. officinale. The RNA extracted from D. officinale culture is used in various analyses. Thermo Fisher Scientific and Invitrogen are used by Waltham, which is associated with USA. The YMC chemical has phases High-DO and Low-DO, and is related to Redox cycle. Chemicals such as glycine, liquid nitrogen, and ABA are used in the analysis of yeast cells.",
